cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: Borkot Tulla
    given-names: MD Hamid
title: >-
  Neural Graph Execution Fingerprints: Software-Only MLaaS Tamper Detection
  via Dual-Channel Mahalanobis Signatures
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-30
url: "https://github.com/hamidborkot/neural-graph-execution-fingerprints"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hamidborkot/neural-graph-execution-fingerprints"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A software-only, zero-hardware MLaaS integrity verification framework that
  detects model tampering, vendor substitution fraud, and adaptive adversarial
  attacks using dual-channel Mahalanobis-distance signatures derived from ONNX
  Runtime execution traces (timing_D) and PyTorch activation statistics
  (activation_D). Runs entirely on Kaggle CPU-only. NDSS submission in preparation.
keywords:
  - MLaaS security
  - model fingerprinting
  - tamper detection
  - execution entropy
  - Mahalanobis distance
  - ONNX Runtime
  - adversarial robustness
  - vendor fraud detection
  - containerized AI security
